            "review_title": "Review at Uchi Sushi",
            "review_text": "Arnewoodian\nNew Forest National Park Hampshire, United Kingdom58 contributions\n0\nBest meal in Vietnam was... japanese!\nMay 2026 • Solo\nI didn't know this was a chain when I ate there. I hope they are all as good as this one on Le Lai was. Quite a small place at street level, easily walked past. Excellent Japanese seafood restaurant, by far the best meal I had in Vietnam (not cheap - but you get what you pay for). Attentive service (but they weren't busy) and a good range of Saki available in half bottles, though you do have to ask for the separate sake menu, otherwise you don't realise. Delicious sashimi, and sushi, it really is much better ordering items separately than the big combo platters, if you know what you're doing. Comfortable 'horseshoe' banquets available upstairs for small groups or just a more private feel.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nOrder separate items to try, not the combo platters, and ask to see the sake list otherwise they don't bring it.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten May 18, 2026",
